From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:39:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] network: spoof opt-in Neo Device-Memory hint natively

Share the base MacBook Neo's 8GB memory value between the native
navigator.deviceMemory getter and the legacy Device-Memory wire hint.
Do not read the host's RAM or inject JavaScript.

Persist case-insensitive Device-Memory Accept-CH opt-in by origin within
each Session, from trustworthy top-level navigation responses (including
redirects and CDP fulfillment). Validate the complete structured token
list and its parameters. Missing/malformed lists preserve the preference;
valid empty/replacement lists remove it.

Generate an unquoted browser-owned HTTP hint before interception and
recompute it after CDP changes/redirects. Respect explicit legacy-header
overrides and the default self policy, using effective origins for
inherited about:blank contexts. Keep WebSocket baseline headers unchanged.
Do not synthesize third-party delegation or other Client Hints.

Avoid replaying stale opt-in after revalidation. Preserve absent Vary
request headers so negotiation from no hint to Device-Memory: 8 cannot
reuse the wrong cached representation; update the existing Vary test.
No new upstream tests are added.

The benchmark previously reported 8 in JavaScript but no header. Temporary
ignored diagnostics cover native getter shape, opt-in/reset, invalid and
parameterized lists, inherited origins, session/origin isolation, insecure
HTTP, CORS, redirects, interception and HTTP caching. All 1658 existing
upstream tests and 54 runtime diagnostics pass in the development build.

References:
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Device-Memory
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/services/network/public/cpp/client_hints.cc
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/main/content/browser/client_hints/client_hints.cc
